sequenceDiagram
    participant S as Sender
    participant R as Receiver<br/>(SentinelHandler)

    rect rgb(255, 235, 235)
    Note over S,R: CURRENT - ASYMMETRIC TRUST (receiver.md M-1, SEVERE).<br/>The module docstring advertises the webhook-auth contract as if it covered ingress;<br/>it covers ONE of two alert routes.

    Note over S,R: ROUTE 1: POST /webhook/generic - HMAC-gated, fail-closed [receiver.py:655, :803]
    S->>R: POST /webhook/generic + X-Sentinel-Timestamp + X-Sentinel-Signature: sha256=<hex>
    R->>R: _webhook_sig_failure_reason(secret, onboarding, headers, body) [receiver.py:121-162]<br/>hex = HMAC-SHA256(secret, "<timestamp>.<raw body>"); |now - ts| <= 300s; hmac.compare_digest<br/>refuses (403) on: empty secret, absent/malformed signature or timestamp,<br/>stale/future-skewed timestamp, bad MAC, legacy timestamp-less signatures.<br/>Startup refuses (SystemExit) on empty secret and on secrets < 16 chars [receiver.py:1176-1183].
    alt check passes
        R->>R: Pipeline.handle_generic -> triage -> page-or-suppress
        R-->>S: 200
    else check fails AND SENTINEL_WEBHOOK_ONBOARDING=1
        Note over R: Onboarding mode fails open LOUDLY: CRITICAL boot warning, per-request WARNING,<br/>webhook_auth_bypassed metric, webhook_auth_fail_open=true on /healthz.
        R->>R: accept, loudly
        R-->>S: 200
    else check fails (production)
        R-->>S: 403 (fail-closed). Nothing forwarded.
    end

    Note over S,R: ROUTE 2: POST /v2/enqueue - TRIGGERS carry NO auth check [receiver.py:652]
    S->>R: POST /v2/enqueue {trigger: critical, dedup_key, summary...} - UNSIGNED
    Note over R: _handle_alert_post calls _signature_ok ONLY for /webhook/generic.<br/>The /v2/enqueue branch goes straight to handle_pd. Headers ride along SOLELY<br/>so resolve/ack CLAIMS can authenticate. There is NO auth gate on this arrow.<br/>Any host with TCP reachability can inject arbitrary triggers with arbitrary<br/>severity, dedup keys, summaries. The only defense is the default --bind 127.0.0.1 -<br/>a network-layer hope, not a trust boundary.
    R->>R: Pipeline.handle_pd(body, headers) -> triage -> page-or-suppress
    R-->>S: 200 (fail-open; unparseable -> forward raw bytes to PD, 200)

    Note over S,R: ROUTE 2b: resolve/ack CLAIMS on /v2/enqueue - the silence direction is fail-closed in EVERY mode
    S->>R: POST /v2/enqueue {event_action: resolve, dedup_key} + HMAC headers
    R->>R: _webhook_sig_failure_reason(secret, False /* onboarding NEVER applies */, headers, body)<br/>[receiver.py:266-284, :302-355 - D10 wiring]
    alt signed claim, known open episode
        R->>R: resolve_episode(fp, reason="verified_resolve") - one of only two legal closes<br/>(operator_resolve; silence NEVER closes)
        R->>R: relay claim to PD unchanged, untriaged
        R-->>S: 200
    else signed claim, unknown/already-closed
        R->>R: idempotent no-op (resolve_noop)
        R-->>S: 200
    else unsigned / bad MAC
        Note over R: An unsigned "resolve" is the false-silence attack (SECURITY.md T1):<br/>refused the close in every mode, including onboarding and secretless startup.<br/>The relay below still happens unchanged - the PD contract is untouched.
        R-->>S: 200 (relay only; episode NOT closed; metric resolve_auth_refused)
    end
    end

    rect rgb(235, 245, 235)
    Note over S,R: REVISED - R-1 (receiver.md section 3 R-1, TYPE 1 for senders; BUILD GATED on Q2).<br/>Apply _webhook_sig_failure_reason in the /v2/enqueue branch BEFORE handle_pd -<br/>reusing the existing pure function, so both routes share ONE scheme.
    S->>R: POST /v2/enqueue + X-Sentinel-Timestamp + X-Sentinel-Signature
    alt valid signature
